  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BACK ON TRACK: PREVENTING TRAIN-ELEPHANT COLLISIONS IN ASSAM, INDIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of this project is to minimize train-elephant collisions in Assam, India and foster the development of Indian Railways systems that prevent train-elephant collisions. Project objectives are to: (1) assess the vulnerabilities of four sections (162 km) of track that account for 75% of prior train-elephant collisions in Assam; (2) provide data-driven recommendations for minimizing the risk of train-elephant collisions in high-risk sections of track; and (3) support the implementation of recommendations to minimize train-elephant collisions. Project activities are to: (1) examine high-risk sections of track via joint surveys with officials from the Railways and Forest Departments; (2) better understand Indian Railways traffic control systems through interviews of railway personnel and direct observations of train control room operations; (3) use video camera traps to monitor elephant crossing points on railroad tracks; (4) make, evaluate, and finalize recommendations to reduce elephant-train collisions via multistakeholder engagements and field visits; (5) revise and finalize recommendations and secure necessary institutional commitment through multi-level stakeholder engagement; (6) conduct workshops with stakeholders to raise awareness of recommendations and implementation plans; and (7) collaborate with key officials as per due process of the Indian Railways and Forest Departments to implement, develop, and test novel interventions.</narrative>
  </description>
